==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|is|bʰuH}}
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|búa}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*būaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpuːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bjó|bjuggu|búið}}

# {{label|is|intransitive}} to [[reside]], to [[live]]{{jump|is|live|s}}
#: ''Ég '''bý''' í Þýskalandi.''
#:: I '''live''' in Germany.
#: ''Þar sem ég '''bý'''.''
#:: In my '''neck of the woods'''.
# {{label|is|intransitive}} to [[run]] a [[farm]] or [[home]]{{jump|is|farm|s}}
#: ''Hann er hættur að '''búa'''.''
#:: He has given up '''farming'''.
# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[prepare]]{{jump|is|prepare|s}}
# {{label|is|impersonal}} used in set phrases
#: ''Honum '''býr''' eitthvað í brjósti.''
#:: There is something on his mind.

